Scarier
=======

Scarier is a lazy AI C++ clone of SCARE, Simon Baldwin's C clone of jAsea,
Mark J. Tilford's Java GPL clone of the Adrift 4 Runner, combined with a lazy
AI C++ clone of the Adrift 5 Runner.  The ADRIFT 5 half was written from a
reading of Campbell Wild's Runner source, as released under the BSD license
in Adrian Welcker's FrankenDrift, and from diffing against FrankenDrift's
output; it uses no code from either.

In other words, it is a single Glk interpreter that plays both ADRIFT 4 and
ADRIFT 5 games.  It is the ADRIFT interpreter in Spatterlight, and the
tree is laid out for that: the Xcode project builds it, and the Makefiles
here are for command-line builds and the regression suites.

Since the fork the ADRIFT 4 half has been measured command by command
against the original 3.7, 3.8, 3.9 and 4.0 Runners (run under Wine, with
transcripts kept in test/adrift4/runner_transcripts/), and the ADRIFT 5 half
against FrankenDrift.  Where Scarier deliberately differs from a Runner --
UNDO, Z, LOOK X and the other conveniences, grammatical text where a Runner
printed an accident -- the deviation is noted in the source.  ChangeLog has
the history; CHANGELOG.md at the top of the Spatterlight tree has the
release notes.


Which engine runs
-----------------

Dispatch happens at load time in glk_main() (glk/os_glk.cpp).
gsc_startup_code() tries the ADRIFT 5 loader first; it returns cleanly on
any non-v5 file, in which case the ADRIFT 4 (SCARE) path takes over.

  * ADRIFT 4 (.taf, v3.7 / v3.8 / v3.9 / v4.0) is handled by the
    SCARE-derived engine: the sc*.cpp sources in core/, the command
    library in library/ and the command runner in runner/.  v4.0 payloads
    are zlib-compressed; v3.7 to v3.9 are XOR-obfuscated with the Visual
    Basic PRNG.  Games whose own data makes them unwinnable are patched as
    they load (core/sctafpar_patches.cpp; `glk patches off` disables).

  * ADRIFT 5 (.taf / .blorb) is handled by the engine in adrift5/: a Blorb
    or raw container whose Exec chunk is XOR-deobfuscated with a fixed
    1024-byte key and zlib-inflated to UTF-8 XML, then parsed into the a5
    object model.  adrift5/run/ is the turn loop and adrift5/text/ the text
    engine.

Both engines share the Glk seam in glk/ (title screens, the map pane,
status line, side windows, media, real-time timer events, saves, the `glk`
meta-commands and the Spatterlight autosave) and the map model and
rasteriser in mapdraw.cpp / core/scmap.cpp; mapdraw.cpp and sessrec.h stay
at the root because both engines use them.  headless/ holds the os-layer stub
(sxstubs.cpp) the headless harnesses link instead of glk/;
platform/ holds the other host layers, os_ansi.cpp (the plain stdout
front end) and scarier-autosave.mm (the Spatterlight autosave bridge the
glk/ seam calls).  tools/ is developer
instrumentation (structural dumps, per-turn traces, the lenient census),
compiled only into the headless walkthrough binary with -DSCARIER_DUMP_TOOLS
and never into a shipping build.

See notes/ADRIFT4_vs_ADRIFT5.md for a detailed comparison of the two code paths
(formats, saves, restriction evaluation, division rounding, and RNG
streams), and notes/ADRIFT-5-XML.md for a specification of the ADRIFT 5
adventure and save formats.


Playing
-------

Both engines understand a family of `glk` meta-commands; `glk help` lists
them and `glk summary` prints the current settings.  Among them: `glk map`
and `glk zoom` for the map pane, `glk colour`, `glk verbose`, `glk notify`,
`glk statusline`, `glk capacity`, `glk patches`, `glk assist` (combat,
move, repeat, room -- the work-arounds some games converted between ADRIFT
versions need; games known to need one get it turned on with a notice at
startup), `glk script`, `glk inputlog` and `glk readlog`, and `glk undo` /
`glk restore` / `glk restart`
/ `glk quit` for when the game's own commands are unavailable.


Building
--------

The default target builds the ANSI/stdout interpreter `scarier`, the one the
golden harness drives; `make glkscarier` builds the Glk interpreter against
the Glk library named by the GLK / GLKDIR variables at the top of Makefile
(terps/cheapglk by default).  The Spatterlight app builds its own copy from
Spatterlight.xcodeproj, target `scarier`:

    make               # ANSI scarier
    make glkscarier    # Glk front end

The sources are C-like C++ (C++11 is enough) and link the system zlib.
The tree also builds with Visual C++ under Windows Glk.


Testing
-------

Makefile.headless builds the standalone test and dump harnesses used for
regression work -- an ANSI/stdout runner plus a family of a5* tools -- and
runs the suites; the engine objects are shared between harnesses and the
suite stages run in parallel.  test/README.md maps the test tree, records
the decisions the 2026 clean-up passes settled and the safety net for any
further change.

    make -f Makefile.headless test           # full suite
    make -f Makefile.headless quick          # the same minus the two
                                             # walkthrough corpora
    make -f Makefile.headless v4walkthroughs # ADRIFT 4 walkthrough replays
    make -f Makefile.headless a5walkthroughs # ADRIFT 5 walkthrough replays
    make -f Makefile.headless a5maptest      # map rendering against goldens
    make -f Makefile.headless sanitize       # ASan/UBSan build of the unit
                                             # harnesses
    make -f Makefile.headless a5run          # headless ADRIFT 5 runner
    make -f Makefile.headless a5dump         # dump decoded v5 XML / model
    make -f Makefile.headless scmap          # headless ADRIFT 4 map dump

The suites that replay real games need the game corpora, which are
third-party and not committed: test/adrift4/games.manifest.tsv and
test/adrift5/games.manifest.tsv pin each file by sha256, and
`sh test/fetch_games.sh fetch` recreates as much of the corpus as is still
online (see test/GAMES.md).  A suite whose corpus is absent is skipped, not
failed.

test/adrift4/ and test/adrift5/ hold the walkthroughs (notes/), the command
scripts and golden transcripts (goldens/), the harnesses (harness/) and the
Runner transcripts and probes the goldens were checked against.  Replays
run with determinism on: SCR_RNG=xoshiro selects the generator that draws
the same stream as a Runner under the vbrng hook, SCR_SEED sets the seed
(1234 by default in that mode), and the SCR_TRACE_* variables turn on the
engine's tracing.  SCR_DEBUGGER_ENABLED=1 enables SCARE's game debugger in
the headless build.

The Spatterlight autosave/autorestore regression lives outside Makefile.
headless because it needs the app's build of the interpreter:

    python3 test/adrift4/harness/run_autosave_tests.py --build

The ADRIFT 5 engine is further validated by diffing headless output
against FrankenDrift (`make -f Makefile.headless test-fd`, opt-in: it
needs dotnet) and by test/adrift5/probes/, a conformance suite of
synthetic games.


License
-------

The Scarier source code is released under the GPL. See COPYING.  The files
derived from SCARE keep its terms, GPL version 2, and carry Simon Baldwin's
and Mark J. Tilford's copyright beside the 2026 line; everything written for
Scarier itself is GPL version 2 or later.
